      trivia: "【A Cigar Born of a Nightclub】The Griffin's is that rare brand born neither on a plantation nor in a factory, but as a bespoke cigar made to entertain the guests of a Geneva discothèque. The master craftsman who rolled its prototype, Hendrik Kelner, met Dr Schneider, Davidoff's owner, in 1988 and drew towards him one of cigar history's turning points: Davidoff's move to Dominican production. The Griffin's, in other words, was also one of the harbingers that led Davidoff from Cuba to the Dominican Republic. For the 25th anniversary in 2009 a limited edition was made in white porcelain jars engraved with the heraldic beast, carrying the club's hedonistic aesthetic down to the present. The American retail catchphrase — “the wallet-friendly Davidoff” — captures this marque's position in a single stroke."
